  "content": {
    "title": "When is the 2026 NFL Draft? Date, start times, TV schedule, channel",
    "text": "March 22, 2026, 12:22 p.m. ETSuper Bowl 60 is over. The first wave of free agency is in the books. Pro days wrap up on the first day of April. It's full steam ahead for the 2026 NFL Draft.All seven rounds of this year's draft will take place over the final full weekend in April. By the end of it all, 257 college football prospects will have landed with their first NFL team. Dozens more will sign on as undrafted free agents, hopeful to make a roster out of training camp.Headlining the class is Heisman Trophy winner, national champion and Indiana quarterback Fernando Mendoza. The presumed No. 1 overall pick is in a league of his own among quarterbacks in this year's draft, with all of the other collegiate signal-callers' draft stocks weighed down by the baggage of a worrying trait or several.Here's everything to know about the 2026 NFL Draft, from when it takes place, to the draft order as well as how to watch on cable and streaming:When is the 2026 NFL Draft?The 2026 NFL Draft will take place between April 23-25 in Pittsburgh.Thursday, April 23: Round 1Friday, April 24: Rounds 2-3Saturday, April 25: Rounds 4-72026 NFL Draft orderOrder via Tankathon for the first round.Las Vegas Raiders: 3-14 record; .538 strength of scheduleNew York Jets: 3-14, .552Arizona Cardinals: 3-14; .571Tennessee Titans: 3-14, .574New York Giants: 4-13; .524Cleveland Browns: 5-12, .486Washington Commanders: 5-12; .507New Orleans Saints: 6-11; .495Kansas City Chiefs: 6-11; .516Cincinnati Bengals: 6-11; .521Miami Dolphins: 7-10; .488Dallas Cowboys: 7-9-1; .438Los Angeles Rams (via Atlanta): 8-9; .495Baltimore Ravens: 8-9; .507Tampa Bay Buccaneers: 8-9, .529New York Jets (via Indianapolis): 8-9; .540Detroit Lions: 9-8; .490Minnesota Vikings: 9-8; .514 SOSCarolina Panthers: 8-9, .522 SOSDallas Cowboys (via Green Bay): 9-7-1; .483Pittsburgh Steelers: 10-7; .503Los Angeles Chargers: 11-6; .469Philadelphia Eagles: 11-6; .476Cleveland Browns (via Jacksonville): 13-4; .478Chicago Bears: 11-6; .458Buffalo Bills: 12-5, .471San Francisco 49ers: 12-5, .498Houston Texans: 12-5; .522Kansas City Chiefs (via Rams): 12-5, .526Miami Dolphins (via Denver): 14-3; .422New England Patriots: 14-3; .391Seattle Seahawks: 14-3; .498How to watch the 2026 NFL DraftDates: April 23-25Time: 8 p.m. ET (Round 1); 7 p.m. ET (Rounds 2-3); Noon ET (Rounds 4-7)Channels: NFL Network; ESPN; ESPN2; ESPN DeportesStreaming: NFL+; ESPN Unlimited & Select; FuboFans have several options to choose from to watch the 2026 NFL Draft. NFL Network and ESPN will have separate broadcasts providing differing analyses on each pick as it happens on draft night.Cord-cutters can stream the different broadcasts on NFL+, the NFL's proprietary streaming service; ESPN Select or ESPN Unlimited, ESPN's streaming services; or cable alternative Fubo, which offers a free trial.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
